  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 224 PM EDT Fri Jul 3 2026\n\nNothing out of the norm weather wise expected for the long term. A \nmidlevel trough will swing through the Ohio/TN Valley between Sunday \nand Monday, likely increasing rain/thunder chances across parts of \nNorth GA during the afternoon. Following the passage of this \nfeature, weak mid-level ridging and surface high pressure will \nremain in place over the western Atlantic extending back into parts \nof the Southeast through most of next week. This will keep a steady \nstream of moisture flow into the region driving daily afternoon rain \nand thunder chances each day. Additionally, temperatures will remain \nquite warm with daily forecast highs in the upper 80s to 90s and \nforecast lows in the 70s (5-10 deg cooler in the mountains). Heat \nindices will follow suit with values expected to hover in the upper \n90s to low 100s over the next 5-7 days.",
